## ADR-32 Renderer mode

**Decision.** Direct2D hardware rendering is the default. PR-001 must also implement the Direct2D software render-target mode. `xtask perf` measures cold launch and idle private bytes in both. If software mode is within 10 percent on frame time for the standard scroll workload and saves more than 5 MB idle, PR-019 flips the default to software. Either way the mode is a setting.

## ADR-33 Startup budget

**Decision.** Before the first frame the process may: parse the CLI, read `settings.toml`, read the keymap, read the session manifest header, create the window and renderer. It may not: restore tabs, read documents, enumerate fonts beyond resolving the editor font family, rasterize icons for hidden toolbars, touch the network, start the extension host, or read recent-file metadata. Session tabs restore incrementally after the first frame, active tab first.

## ADR-34 License

**Decision.** Application and core crates: **MPL-2.0** (file-level copyleft: changes to Bareline files must be shared; combining with other code, including proprietary extensions, is allowed). Extension SDK, protocol crates and first-party extensions: **MIT OR Apache-2.0**. The name "Bareline", the logo and the icon are trademarks of the owner and are not covered by the code license; forks must rename. Third-party notices are generated by `cargo about`. Switching the core to Apache-2.0 OR MIT later is a one-line change if the owner prefers maximum permissiveness.

## ADR-35 Signing

**Decision.** Windows Authenticode through SignPath Foundation (free for open-source projects) with Azure Trusted Signing as fallback. Update manifests and release checksums are signed with a minisign ed25519 key held offline by the owner; the public key is embedded in the binary; rotation procedure documented in `SECURITY.md`.

## ADR-36 Governance and process

**Decision.** Owner-led project with a maintainers file. Contributions require DCO sign-off, not a CLA. GitHub Actions CI. Monthly minor releases, patch releases as needed. Private vulnerability reporting through GitHub. No telemetry. Details in `06_OPEN_SOURCE_AND_DISTRIBUTION.md`.

## ADR-37 Text/raw domains and codec provenance

**Problem.** v1.1 tried to encode invalid source bytes as special Unicode values, violating the valid text view and colliding with real characters.

**Decision.** Use U+FFFD display spans plus an original-byte side table under FC-01.

**Consequences.** Pay for mapping storage and atomic invalid-span edits; replace in-band byte escaping and preserve genuine U+FFFD/private-use text.

## ADR-38 Bounded sources, newline aggregates and storage budgets

**Problem.** v1.1 allowed whole decoded files and per-tab caches to exhaust RAM and counted LF alone.

**Decision.** Use bounded sources, CR/LF/CRLF aggregates and disk-backed transcode storage under FC-02.

**Consequences.** Pay disk I/O and quota handling costs; replace in-memory transcode accumulation and report unknown indexes until verified.

## ADR-39 Durable recovery and baseline availability

**Problem.** v1.1 let undo depend on evictable source pages and confused journaled edits with a complete recovery baseline.

**Decision.** Own inverse bytes before transaction commit and publish durability only after ordered segment/journal flushes under FC-03.

**Consequences.** Pay copy, disk and sealing costs; replace view-page retention with owned segments and expose Complete versus Edits only recovery.

## ADR-40 Save, tail continuity and filesystem semantics

**Problem.** v1.1 treated rename as universally atomic and append notifications as proof that the old prefix survived.

**Decision.** Revalidate captured save state, source continuity and filesystem capabilities under FC-04.

**Consequences.** Pay identity checks, metadata preservation and fallback-copy work; replace unconditional replace and tail-append assumptions.

## ADR-41 Complete search and revalidated workspace replacement

**Problem.** v1.1 inspected pattern strings to guess multiline behavior and could replace a newer file using an obsolete preview.

**Decision.** Use bounded regex context with explicit completeness and revalidate reviewed fingerprints before replacement under FC-05.

**Consequences.** Pay retained-context, compatibility-fixture and receipt costs; drop the pattern-string multiline heuristic because syntax alone cannot prove streamed match correctness.

## ADR-42 Logical actors, linked undo and bounded diff

**Problem.** v1.1 assigned one thread per document and left linked undo and huge diff output unbounded.

**Decision.** Schedule logical actors on a shared bounded pool and coordinate linked mutations and bounded diff output under FC-06.

**Consequences.** Pay mailbox backpressure, revision coordination and coarse-result handling; replace per-document threads so thousands of tabs share a fixed worker budget.

## ADR-43 Extension capabilities, lifecycle and offline contracts

**Problem.** v1.1 conflated disabled extensions with absent runtime files and left early consumers without a verified package interface.

**Decision.** Separate disable from Remove runtime and enforce verified providers and per-extension grants under FC-07.

**Consequences.** Retain installed disk bytes for offline reuse after disable; reclaim them only on Remove runtime, and pay capability, IPC and offline-verification costs.

## ADR-44 Release trust, rollback protection and signing ceremony

**Problem.** v1.1 promised reproducible signed artifacts and omitted rollback, freshness and compromised-key recovery limits.

**Decision.** Require a reproducible unsigned payload and authenticated release/update metadata under FC-08.

**Consequences.** Pay two clean payload builds and signing ceremony work; replace the blanket reproducible-build claim because timestamped signatures and final containers vary.

## ADR-45 Platform floor, path fidelity and workspace trust

**Problem.** v1.1 left Windows compatibility floors, lossless path persistence and workspace privilege limits implicit.

**Decision.** Use explicit platform floors, tagged lossless paths and restricted workspace settings under FC-09.

**Consequences.** Pay platform fixtures and policy validation; replace lossy display-path identity and unrestricted workspace overrides.

## ADR-46 Reproducible benchmark method and claim boundaries

**Problem.** v1.1 collapsed launch/load milestones and assumed the comparison editor would fail huge-file workloads.

**Decision.** Measure independent milestones, paired raw samples and completion or timeout under FC-10.

**Consequences.** Pay controlled repetitions and environment capture; replace unsupported superiority claims while retaining informational performance budgets.

## ADR-47 Windows-first qualification and bounded limits

**Authority/date.** Owner delegated product decisions on 2026-09-16 and explicitly deferred Linux/macOS testing to the next update.

**Decision.** Target Windows x64 now; maintain the documented platform floors pending clean-machine proof. Preserve bounded encoding, search, recovery, line-index and accessibility behavior under FC-02/03/05/09. Treat extra low-integrity/AppContainer isolation and broad module restructuring as future hardening/maintenance, without misrepresenting the implemented boundary. See `docs/implementation/production-readiness/KNOWN-LIMITS-20260916.md` for evidence and owners.

**Consequences.** No mock or Windows-only run qualifies a foreign host, physical accessibility, signed deployment or 72-hour operation. Required independent acceptance and all P0/P1 reliability/security release gates remain. This is scope disposition, not evidence that pending qualification passed.
